  "characterBrief": "Keep a neutral, polite tone. Do not correct or grade the candidate. Say each sentence and question once, then give the candidate time to respond. Move on when time is up. The mock should take about five minutes.\n\nListen and Repeat\nThe candidate is starting a tour of the science building. A guide speaks each sentence, and the candidate repeats it.\nOpening line, say once: Hello, I'm Sarah. First, listen to each sentence and repeat it exactly. You're starting a tour of the science building. Welcome to the science building.\n1. Welcome to the science building. This sentence is already included in the opening line. Do not say it again.\n2. The lab is on your left.\n3. Please leave your bags beside the door.\n4. You can use this room when your class needs a quiet place to work.\n5. The study area is upstairs, where students can read or work together between their classes.\n6. If you need a book, ask the staff member who usually sits beside the front desk.\n7. The computer room stays open after class, so students who need more time can finish their assignments there.\n\nTake an Interview\nA researcher is studying how students use the library. Say: Now, I'll ask you a few questions about using the library. Please answer each question as fully as you can. You can speak for up to about 45 seconds.\n1. How often do you visit a library?\n2. Tell me about a time you studied or read in a library. What did you do there?\n3. Do you think students learn better in a library or at home? Why?\n4. In the future, how do you think students will use libraries differently?\n\nThere are no follow-up questions. Thank the candidate briefly when the interview is finished.",
  "objectives": [
    {
      "label": "Listen and Repeat",
      "description": "Repita exatamente sete frases que ouvir em um passeio pelo prédio de ciências."
    },
    {
      "label": "Take an Interview",
      "description": "Responda a quatro perguntas sobre experiências e opiniões relacionadas ao uso da biblioteca."
    }
  ],
  "openingLine": "Hello, I'm Sarah. First, listen to each sentence and repeat it exactly. You're starting a tour of the science building. Welcome to the science building.",
  "hints": [
    "I think this is a good idea.",
    "One reason is that it helps people learn.",
    "For example, I worked with a friend once.",
    "In the future, I think students will use it more."
  ]
}

{
  "title": "IELTS Speaking Practice Mock",
  "situation": "You will complete a five-minute practice mock of the IELTS Speaking test, shorter than the real 11-to-14-minute test. This is not a real or official test.",
